<article class="env-corollary" id="314AE8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/314AE8">Corollary <span data-tag="314AE8">4.1.1.13</span>.</a> Let $p: S \rightarrow S'$ be a cofinal map, and $K$ any simplicial set. Then the induced map $K \times S \rightarrow K \times S'$ is cofinal. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollary <a href="/tag/BEC80D" data-tag="BEC80D">4.1.1.12</a>, we may suppose that $p$ is either right anodyne or a trivial fibration. Then the induced map $K \times S \rightarrow K \times S'$ has the same property. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>